Below is a production-grade, zero-downtime CI/CD approach for deploying a Spring Boot app on Azure, very similar in rigor to what you’d design for AWS/GCP.

I’ll explain architecture → deployment strategy → CI/CD pipeline → rollback, with concrete Azure services.

---

 1️⃣ Recommended Azure Architecture (Zero Downtime)

 Option A (Most Common & Simple): Azure App Service + Deployment Slots

Best if you don’t need Kubernetes.

```
GitHub / Azure DevOps
        |
   CI Pipeline
        |
 Build JAR + Tests
        |
   CD Pipeline
        |
 Azure App Service
   ├── Production Slot (live traffic)
   └── Staging Slot (new version)
```

Azure handles traffic switching atomically → zero downtime.

---

 Option B (Enterprise / High Scale): AKS + Blue-Green or Canary

Use if you already run Kubernetes.

```
GitHub Actions
      |
 Build Docker Image
      |
 Push to Azure Container Registry (ACR)
      |
 AKS
  ├── v1 (Blue)
  └── v2 (Green)
        |
   Azure Load Balancer / Ingress
```

---

For 90% of Spring Boot apps, Option A (App Service + Slots) is ideal.

