 2️⃣ Disaster Recovery — Multi-Region AKS (Real Production)

 🎯 Goal

Survive:

 Region outage
 Network partition
 Cluster failure

---

 🔹 Multi-Region Active-Passive (Most Common)

```
              ┌───────────────┐
              │ Azure Front   │
              │ Door (Global) │
              └───────────────┘
                   |
        ┌──────────┴──────────┐
        |                     |
┌───────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐
│ AKS - Region A│     │ AKS - Region B│
│ (Primary)     │     │ (Standby)     │
└───────────────┘     └───────────────┘
        |
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│ Primary DB + Geo-Replication │
└──────────────────────────────┘
```

---

 🔹 Failover Flow

1. Front Door health probe fails
2. Traffic shifts to Region B
3. AKS already warm
4. DB promoted (if needed)

⏱ RTO: minutes
📉 RPO: seconds (depends on DB)

---

 🔹 Active-Active (Advanced / Expensive)

```
Front Door
   |
   +--> AKS Region A
   |
   +--> AKS Region B
```

Used only when:

 Ultra-low latency required
 Data layer supports multi-write (Cosmos DB, Spanner-like)

